---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Dama Image Prep"
  description="Why Dama Image Prep exists, what it does and how its technical guides are produced."
  activeNav="/about/"
  ><header class="legal-hero legal-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">DAMA IMAGE PREP</p><h1>About Dama Image Prep</h1>
  </header><section class="legal-content legal-shell">
    <p>
      Dama Image Prep is an independent browser-based utility for small sellers
      who repeatedly prepare product photos. It brings canvas sizing, padding,
      crop checks, naming and ZIP export into one workspace.
    </p><h2>A deliberately small scope</h2><p>
      This is not an image retouching suite, background-removal service or
      marketplace integration. It does not upload your photos, manage listings
      or promise marketplace acceptance. It preserves your original files and
      creates separate exports.
    </p><h2>Who creates the site</h2><p>
      The site is maintained under the Dama Image Prep name. Technical guides
      and software may be developed with AI assistance and are reviewed against
      the implemented workflow and cited documentation. The editorial name does
      not represent a claimed team of professional photographers or first-hand
      seller experience.
    </p><h2>Useful explanations, not invented credentials</h2><p>
      Our examples are illustrative calculations, checklists and framing
      diagrams. We do not invent testimonials, sales results, user counts or
      personal experience. Platform references link to their original
      documentation; our presets are independent starting points.
    </p><h2>Funding and independence</h2><p>
      The workspace is free to use. The site may seek advertising support, but
      the current version does not load advertising or analytics scripts.
      Advertising approval and revenue are not guaranteed. Dama is not
      affiliated with Etsy, Shopify or Google.
    </p><p>
      <a href="/standards/">Read the methods and limitations</a> or <a
        href="/contact/">report a problem</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section></BaseLayout
>
